    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All tests pass. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## What I did \u2014 soft-delete for owners\n\n**Behaviour change:** `DELETE /api/owners/{id}` now flags the owner `deleted=true` and keeps the row (returns 2xx); `GET` still returns it with `deleted` true; a new owner is `deleted` false; and the create endpoint's duplicate/identity checks skip deleted owners.\n\n**Files touched (7), each edit small and localized:**\n\n1. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `deleted` field (`Boolean`, defaulting to `Boolean.FALSE`) with a plain getter/setter. New cohesive members, no existing method modified.\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `deleted` boolean to the `Owner` response schema; MapStruct maps it automatically from the entity, so the mapper was untouched.\n3. **`function/owner/DeleteOwner.java`** \u2014 `service` now sets `deleted=true` and `save`s instead of `delete`ing (2 lines).\n4. **`function/owner/RejectDuplicateOwnerIdentity.java`** \u2014 one extra guard `&& !Boolean.TRUE.equals(other.getDeleted())` in the match condition.\n5. **`function/owner/RejectDuplicateOwnerHousehold.java`** \u2014 same one-condition guard.\n6. **`db/hsqldb/schema.sql`** \u2014 added `deleted BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE` (the test profile is hsqldb with `ddl-auto=none`).\n7. **`db/hsqldb/data.sql`** \u2014 appended `FALSE` to the 10 positional seed inserts so they match the new column.\n\n**Structural-impact notes:** every function I changed is a single-method function class (`WMC_other = 1`), so no edit pays for a large surrounding class \u2014 I deliberately kept the two duplicate checks as one-line condition additions rather than extracting shared logic, and used MapStruct's by-name mapping to avoid touching `OwnerMapper` or `RespondWithOwner`. I left h2/mysql/postgres schemas alone: h2 uses `ddl-auto=update` (column auto-added) and mysql/postgres already omit the entity's extra columns by existing convention.\n\nI only left one thing worth flagging: seed owners loaded before the column had a value would read `null`, but the checks use `Boolean.TRUE.equals(...)` so `null` is safely treated as not-deleted, and the hsqldb schema default keeps seed rows `FALSE`.",
